(
 '* 1.2.0 ⋄ 2026-09-17'
 '  * Dependency `CommTools` updated to 3.2.0'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * `Status` showed mutilated drawing chars'
 '* 1.1.0 ⋄ 2026-09-13'
 '  * Commit improved: now -amend can be executed without adding a single file, but the user might'
 '    still also quit the whole operation by enterin "q". '
 '  * Status provided a much more readable result with the -view option'
 '  * Several syntax changes in the way CommTools.Select is called due to breaking changes in 3.0.0'
 '* 1.0.1 ⋄ 2026-09-11'
 '  * CompareCommits and CompareVersions both... '
 '    * take staged changes into account as well now'
 '    * do handle renamed APL objects now '
 '  * `]ChangeLog` and `]ShowLastVersionInIndex` accept filenames as well as APL names'
 '  * `project_url` in the package config file corrected: ws still pointing to APLGit'
 '  * Internal changes in order to get rid of technical debt.'
 '* 1.0.0 ⋄ 2026-09-01'
 '  * Promoted to version 1.0    '
 '  * `]CompareVersions` added'
 '  * `]CompareCommits` now tells the user which commits it compares, and no longer fails on main/master'
 '  * acre support: all Link-specific calls now go via `GetFileName`/`GetItemName`, and both fall back to acre'
 '  * `]Add`: comma-separated file lists now work, and specifying an APL object no longer crashes'
 '  * One rule for file arguments: relative to the root of the project (see `]Add -??`), and a bare name is searched for in the source folder'
 '  * API function `CompareVersions` added; `]CompareVersions` is now a thin layer on top of it'
 '  * ]Version now also reports which namespace the user commands execute their code in'
 '  * Folders are now normalised in one place (`U.NormalizeFolder`): slashes, and no trailing separator'
 '  * New version of `CommTools` makes file selection in `]Commit` much easier in some circumstances tx to'
 '    the new `a~{n}`-syntax.'
 '  * Bug fix: `]ChangeLog` had a problem and showed long date when it shouldn''t                      '
 '* 0.31.0 ⋄ 2026-08-17'
 '  * ]StashShow got deleted. There are way to many options etc. to make this useful from APL. '
 '    To be used from a Git Bash instead.'
 '  * ]Status has changed, including its syntax          '
 '    * -APLnames removed from ]Status : including them is now the default'
 '    * -noAPLnames: use this to suppress the APL names                                             '
 '  * New command ]StashListContent added. List all files, including untracked ones, that got captured'
 '    in a stash.'
 '  * ]CompareCommits now allows to compare the working area not only with the latest commit but any'
 '  * Level-1-Help does not replicate information anymore but cites the source.'
 '  * Help page for StashList corrected.  '
 '  * RunProcess now returns StdErr in one and the same shape no matter which branch it took'
 '  * ]RefLog is now branch-aware: -branch= used to be accepted but silently ignored, it now'
 '    lists the reflog of the given branch. The API function takes (restrictFlag branch) as ⍵;'
 '    passing just the restrict flag, as before, still works.'
 '  * User command help checked and polished throughout:'
 '    * ]Status had it the wrong way round: the SHORT report is the default, not the long one'
 '    * ]Repack never passed -a, -d and -f on to Git because they were not part of the'
 '      command''s "Parse" string; they are gone now, from both the help and the code'
 '    * Options that were missing from the help added: ]StashPop -n=, ]RefLog -project=,'
 '      ]GetTagOfLatestRelease -username= and the syntax of ]Diff -op='
 '    * Several wrong or misspelled command descriptions corrected, among them ]Version, which'
 '      returns a text vector and not a three-element vector'
 '    * Five help pages (Add, ChangeLog, CloneRepo, Repack, StashPush) used the vector'
 '      notation introduced with Dyalog 20.0 and therefore did not load at all on 18.x and 19.x.'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * Bug fix: the temp file used to catch StdErr survived when ⎕SH threw an error.   '
 '    * ]GetTagOfLatestRelease was broken in three different ways    '
 '* 0.30.1 ⋄ 2026-07-20'
 '  * Bug fix: Commit did not handle all circumstances with -amend correctly '
 '* 0.30.0 ⋄ 2026-07-15'
 '  * CloneRepo added'
 '  * CompareCommits did not handle files having acre-specific filenames'
)
